{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>But only to the place that YHWH your Elohim shall choose from all your tribes.</b> This place is Mount Moriah, and it was known and renowned among the nations, for they knew of its excellence through tradition — needless to say Israel in the wilderness, who knew this from the patriarchs, since the binding of Isaac took place there. And the reason Scripture left this place unspecified and did not explicitly say that it is Mount Moriah, renowned and famous to all — the Rambam, of blessed memory, wrote in the Guide for the Perplexed that the concealment of the place was for three reasons. The first: had the nations known that prayer is accepted there and that sacrifices there find favor, every nation would seek to lay hold of it, and strife and bloodshed among the nations would multiply. The second: the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land — since they knew that Israel was destined to inherit their land and to serve the Blessed Name and to offer their sacrifices in that place — they would have destroyed it by every means possible. The third: the tribes would have quarreled with one another, each and every one seeking to have that place in his own inheritance, and strife and dissension would break out among them, just as it broke out over the pursuit of the priesthood. Therefore Scripture concealed and left unspecified this place and did not make it known — and needless to say the nations, for even Israel did not know it; for even though all knew of the excellence of Mount Moriah, they did not know that it was the place that YHWH would choose." "<b>To His dwelling you shall seek.</b> For the glory of Him who dwells there shall you seek. And from here our Rabbis of blessed memory said: Shekhinah is named on account of glory (kavod), in the manner of what is said (Exodus 24): ״וישכן כבוד ה׳ על הר סיני״ — 'and the glory of YHWH dwelt upon Mount Sinai'; and likewise (Psalms 85): ״לשכון כבוד בארצנו״ — 'that glory may dwell in our land.' And it says this concerning Shiloh."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:54.861739919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}